# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a first run without the QPU, set **Quantum Source** to `random`, which runs the solver jobs on uniform random bitstrings. To sample through IBM Quantum Platform (IQP) from the workflow host instead of a Slurm job, save a `QrmiRuntimeBlock` with `scheduler = \"iqp\"` (the `[runtime]` table of `sqd_blocks.toml`, in place of `[qrmi]`), and name it in **QRMI Runtime Block**. This block reads the API key from the `qrmi_config.json` file of the workflow host.\n"
msgstr "Para uma primeira execução sem a QPU, defina **Quantum Source** como `random`, que executa os jobs do solver em bitstrings aleatórias uniformes. Para amostrar pelo IBM Quantum Platform (IQP) a partir do host do workflow em vez de um job Slurm, salve um `QrmiRuntimeBlock` com `scheduler = \"iqp\"` (a tabela `[runtime]` de `sqd_blocks.toml`, no lugar de `[qrmi]`) e informe o nome dele em **QRMI Runtime Block**. Esse bloco lê a chave de API do arquivo `qrmi_config.json` do host do workflow.\n"

